  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The young but promising paparazzi Gennady wants to finally become famous. To do this, he wants to take a picture of a new super star during her walk in the mountains.\n\nIt is known that the star's path in the mountains consists of NNN sections. For each valid iii, the iii-th section is a vertical half-open interval with coordinates x=ix = ix=i and y∈[0,hi)y \\in [0, h_i)y∈[0,hi​).\n\nFor each valid iii and jjj, our hero can take a picture of the star located in the iii-th section of the walk when he is in the jjj-th section only if he can see the star ― that is, i&lt;ji \\lt ji&lt;j and for each kkk (i&lt;k&lt;ji \\lt k \\lt ji&lt;k&lt;j), the half-open interval that makes up the kkk-th section must not intersect the line segment [(i,hi),(j,hj)][(i, h_i), (j, h_j)][(i,hi​),(j,hj​)].\n\nGennady is a paparazzi, not a programmer, so he asks you to determine the maximum distance from which he can take a picture of the star, which is the maximum value of j−ij-ij−i over all pairs (i,j)(i, j)(i,j). Help him become famous!",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤5⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 5 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤5⋅105",
      "1≤hi≤1091 \\leq h_i \\leq 10^91≤hi​≤109 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):** the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 500500500",
      "**Subtask #2 (10 points):** the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 8,0008,0008,000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers h1,h2,…,hNh_1, h_2, \\ldots, h_Nh1​,h2​,…,hN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the maximum distance.",
